{"toolCallId":"call_1790fa71d45d4b898855373db2ad3f6d","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: CHECK-GREP-CONVENTION\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Sourced by validate.sh and compatible with strict mode.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Rule: GREP_CONVENTION\n# Severity: error\n# Description: Checks markdown documents against the greppable-corpus\n#   convention. Anchor grammar is checked here for the corpus contract; ANCHORS_VALID in the orchestrator checks pairing and order.\n# convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and\n# naming. Classification lives in the node helper because bash cannot parse\n# YAML honestly.\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nGREP_CONVENTION_HELPER=\"${GREP_CONVENTION_HELPER:-$SCRIPT_DIR/check-grep-convention-helper.mjs}\"\n\nrun_check() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local _level=\"$2\"\n    local rule_id=\"GREP_CONVENTION\"\n\n    RULE_NAME=\"$rule_id\"\n    RULE_STATUS=\"pass\"\n    RULE_MESSAGE=\"\"\n    RULE_DETAILS=()\n    RULE_REMEDIATION=\"\"\n\n    if [[ ! -f \"$GREP_CONVENTION_HELPER\" ]]; then\n        RULE_STATUS=\"fail\"\n        RULE_MESSAGE=\"Grep convention helper missing\"\n        RULE_DETAILS=(\"Expected helper: $GREP_CONVENTION_HELPER\")\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    local output=\"\"\n    if ! output=\"$(node \"$GREP_CONVENTION_HELPER\" \"$folder\" \"$rule_id\" 2>&1)\"; then\n        RULE_STATUS=\"fail\"\n        RULE_MESSAGE=\"Grep convention helper failed to run\"\n        RULE_DETAILS=(\"$output\")\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    local kind value\n    while IFS=$'\\t' read -r kind value; do\n        [[ -z \"${kind:-}\" ]] && continue\n        case \"$kind\" in\n            rule) RULE_NAME=\"$value\" ;;\n            status) RULE_STATUS=\"$value\" ;;\n            message) RULE_MESSAGE=\"$value\" ;;\n            detail) RULE_DETAILS+=(\"$value\") ;;\n        esac\n    done <<< \"$output\"\n\n    if [[ -z \"$RULE_MESSAGE\" ]]; then\n        RULE_STATUS=\"fail\"\n        RULE_MESSAGE=\"Grep convention rule bridge returned no parseable output\"\n        RULE_DETAILS=(\"Raw output: $output\")\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    if [[ \"$RULE_STATUS\" != \"pass\" ]]; then\n        RULE_REMEDIATION=\"Repair the reported documents: give each one a conforming frontmatter block, replace generic trigger phrases with author-controlled terms, and pair every anchor marker.\"\n    fi\n\n    return 0\n}\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"a17e8c","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_1e7d0b4c63a94c74a4549b3553ff6c16","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Graph Scripts: Metadata Backfill And Migration\"\ndescription: \"CLI helpers for refreshing and migrating spec-folder graph-metadata and description.json files across the specs tree.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"graph metadata backfill\"\n  - \"backfill graph metadata\"\n  - \"spec graph metadata\"\n  - \"migrate generated json\"\n---\n\n# Graph Scripts: Metadata Backfill And Migration\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`runtime/cli/graph/` contains the CLI entrypoints that refresh and migrate `graph-metadata.json` and `description.json` files for spec folders. It discovers packet folders, derives current metadata, and reports low-confidence fields or drift that may need review.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- `backfill-graph-metadata.ts` defaults to an inclusive scan of active, archived, and future spec trees.\n- `backfill-graph-metadata.ts` supports `--active-only` when archived paths should be skipped.\n- Both entrypoints support `--dry-run` for previewing created, refreshed, and flagged packets.\n- `migrate-generated-json.ts` regenerates both generated files per folder in isolation, and supports a `--prune-report` / `--prune --prune-confirm` two-step flow for removing stale artifacts.\n\n---\n\n## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\ngraph/\n+-- backfill-graph-metadata.ts\n`-- migrate-generated-json.ts\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `backfill-graph-metadata.ts` | Collects spec folders and calls graph metadata derivation or refresh APIs. |\n| `migrate-generated-json.ts` | Enumerates every spec folder and regenerates `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` per folder, with dry-run, scoped `--only`/`--root`, and a hash-confirmed prune flow. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. ENTRYPOINTS\n\nRun the built scripts from the repository root:\n\n```bash\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js --dry-run\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js --active-only\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/migrate-generated-json.js --dry-run --verify\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/migrate-generated-json.js --only <spec-folder>\n```\n\nUse `--root <specs-dir>` to target a specific specs directory.\n\n---\n\n## 5. BOUNDARIES\n\nThe scripts own graph metadata and description regeneration only. They should not edit authored spec documents such as `spec.md`, `plan.md`, or `implementation-summary.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED\n\n- `../config/README.md`\n- `../../runtime/api/`\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"6dc46a","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_204b05c0ed784f8c844fe9bc65f9e465","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"FILE_EXISTS | error |  | Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\nPLACEHOLDER_FILLED | error |  | Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\nCOMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER | error |  | Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\nSCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED | error |  | Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\nSTATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY | error |  | Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\nLEVEL_DECLARED | info |  | Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\nAC_COVERAGE | info |  | Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\nAC_CLOSURE | error |  | Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\nANCHORS_VALID | error |  | Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. Template order is not checked.\nFRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK | error |  | Validates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\nMERGE_LEGALITY | error |  | Validates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\nSPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY | error |  | Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\nCROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION | error |  | Detects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\nPOST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT | error |  | Verifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\nTOC_POLICY | error |  | Enforces table-of-contents placement policy.\nAI_PROTOCOLS | error |  | Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\nCOMPLEXITY_MATCH | error |  | Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\nFOLDER_NAMING | error |  | Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\nFRONTMATTER_VALID | error |  | Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\nFRONTMATTER_VALUES | warn |  | Warns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list in sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json. Aliases are legal.\nSOURCE_TAGS | warn |  | Warns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or review artifacts names a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, using sk-doc's citation resolver. Packets created on or before the cutoff are skipped. A pass means the path and line exist, not that they support the claim.\nGREP_CONVENTION | error |  | Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\nLEVEL_MATCH | error |  | Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\nGRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT | warn |  | Checks generated description and graph metadata are present.\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT | warn |  | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY | error |  | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the packet's own current identity (stale rename residue the refresh writer now prunes).\nGRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE | warn |  | Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\nMETADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY | error |  | Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\nDESCRIPTION_SHAPE | warn |  | Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\nNORMALIZER_LINT | error |  | Strict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\nSPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY | error |  | Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\nTEMPLATE_SOURCE | error |  | Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED | error |  | Checks canonical save packet identity normalization.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS | error |  | Checks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\nCONTINUITY_FRESHNESS | error | strict | Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\nGENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY | error | strict | Validates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants, error under strict behind a grandfather report mode.\nGENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT | error | strict | Re-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and the current docs, read-only, error under strict only when the drift-gate flag is on and otherwise grandfather report mode.\nLINKS_VALID | warn |  | Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"376805","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_22e27c5f911d4bc182fc10c75188885c","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"            if (line ~ /^[[:space:]]*#{1,6}[[:space:]]*\\*{0,2}[Aa][Dd][Rr]-[0-9]+/ ||\n                line ~ /^[[:space:]]*[-*][[:space:]]*\\*{0,2}[Aa][Dd][Rr]-[0-9]+/ ||\n                line ~ /^[[:space:]]*\\|[[:space:]]*\\*{0,2}[Aa][Dd][Rr]-[0-9]+/) {\n                if (match(line, /[Aa][Dd][Rr]-[0-9]+/)) print toupper(substr(line, RSTART, RLENGTH))\n            }\n        }\n    ' \"$dr_file\"\n}\n\n# Zero padding is not significant: a waiver and the record it cites may write\n# the same number differently.\n_acc_adr_key() {\n    printf 'ADR-%s' \"$(printf '%s' \"${1#*-}\" | sed 's/^0*//;s/^$/0/')\"\n}\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 3. VALIDATION LOGIC\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nrun_check() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local level=\"$2\"\n\n    RULE_NAME=\"AC_CLOSURE\"\n    RULE_STATUS=\"pass\"\n    RULE_MESSAGE=\"\"\n    RULE_DETAILS=()\n    RULE_REMEDIATION=\"\"\n\n    _ACC_FLAG_NOTE=\"\"\n    _ACC_CUTOFF_NOTE=\"\"\n\n    if ! _acc_enabled; then\n        RULE_MESSAGE=\"Acceptance closure gate disabled (set SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=true to enable)\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    local level_num\n    level_num=\"$(_acc_numeric_level \"$level\")\"\n    [[ -z \"$level_num\" ]] && level_num=1\n\n    if [[ \"$level_num\" -lt 2 ]]; then\n        RULE_MESSAGE=\"Acceptance closure gate not active below Level 2\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    local ac_file=\"$folder/acceptance-criteria.md\"\n    local dr_file=\"$folder/decision-record.md\"\n    local cutoff created pre_cutoff=false\n\n    cutoff=\"$(_acc_cutoff_date)\"\n    if ! created=\"$(_acc_created_date \"$folder/spec.md\")\"; then\n        pre_cutoff=true\n        created=\"unknown\"\n    elif [[ ! \"$created\" > \"$cutoff\" ]]; then\n        # On the cutoff date itself the packet is still grandfathered: the\n        # boundary day belongs to the world that existed before the gate.\n        pre_cutoff=true\n    fi\n\n    [[ -n \"$_ACC_FLAG_NOTE\" ]] && RULE_DETAILS+=(\"$_ACC_FLAG_NOTE\")\n    [[ -n \"$_ACC_CUTOFF_NOTE\" ]] && RULE_DETAILS+=(\"$_ACC_CUTOFF_NOTE\")\n\n    # Grandfathered packets are advisory on EVERY branch, not just presence.\n    local verdict=\"fail\"\n    $pre_cutoff && verdict=\"info\"\n\n    if [[ ! -f \"$ac_file\" ]]; then\n        if $pre_cutoff; then\n            RULE_STATUS=\"info\"\n            RULE_MESSAGE=\"acceptance-criteria.md absent; packet created ${created} is at or before the ${cutoff} cutoff, so closure is advisory\"\n            return 0\n        fi\n        RULE_STATUS=\"fail\"\n        RULE_MESSAGE=\"acceptance-criteria.md is required at Level ${level} for packets created after ${cutoff} (this packet: ${created})\"\n        RULE_REMEDIATION=\"Scaffold it from templates/addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl and list the criteria this packet must satisfy.\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    local declared_adrs=\"\"\n    local adr\n    while IFS= read -r adr; do\n        [[ -z \"$adr\" ]] && continue\n        declared_adrs=\"$declared_adrs $(_acc_adr_key \"$adr\")\"\n    done < <(_acc_declared_adrs \"$dr_file\")\n\n    local unmet=() dangling=() malformed=() seen_ids=\"\" dupes=()\n    local total=0 met=0\n    local id status waiver status_l key cited missing\n\n    while IFS=$'\\t' read -r id status waiver; do\n        [[ -z \"$id\" ]] && continue\n        if [[ \"$id\" == \"MALFORMED\" ]]; then\n            malformed+=(\"${status}: ${waiver}\")\n            continue\n        fi\n        case \" $seen_ids \" in\n            *\" $id \"*) dupes+=(\"$id\") ;;\n            *) seen_ids=\"$seen_ids $id\" ;;\n        esac\n        total=$((total + 1))\n        status_l=\"$(_acc_lower \"$status\")\"\n        case \"$status_l\" in\n            met)\n                met=$((met + 1))\n                ;;\n            waived|superseded)\n                cited=\"$(printf '%s' \"$waiver\" | grep -Eoi 'ADR-[0-9]+' || true)\"\n                if [[ -z \"$cited\" ]]; then\n                    dangling+=(\"$id is ${status} but names no decision record\")\n                    continue\n                fi\n                missing=\"\"\n                while IFS= read -r adr; do\n                    [[ -z \"$adr\" ]] && continue\n                    key=\"$(_acc_adr_key \"$(_acc_lower \"$adr\" | tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]')\")\"\n                    case \" $declared_adrs \" in\n                        *\" $key \"*) ;;\n                        *) missing=\"$missing ${adr}\" ;;\n                    esac\n                done <<< \"$cited\"\n                if [[ -n \"$missing\" ]]; then\n                    dangling+=(\"$id cites${missing}, not declared in decision-record.md\")\n                else\n                    met=$((met + 1))\n                fi\n                ;;\n            *)\n                unmet+=(\"$id (${status:-blank})\")\n                ;;\n        esac\n    done < <(_acc_rows \"$ac_file\")\n\n    # A row that could not be parsed is never treated as absent: an emptied\n    # table would otherwise report a closeable packet.\n    if [[ ${#malformed[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then\n        RULE_STATUS=\"$verdict\"\n        RULE_MESSAGE=\"AC_CLOSURE: ${#malformed[@]} criterion row(s) could not be parsed\"\n        RULE_DETAILS+=(\"${malformed[@]}\")\n        RULE_REMEDIATION=\"Use the template's table shape: an AC-ID header row, one AC-NNN per row, and balanced code fences.\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    if [[ \"$total\" -eq 0 ]]; then\n        RULE_STATUS=\"info\"\n        RULE_MESSAGE=\"acceptance-criteria.md present but lists no criteria; closure gate is a no-op\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n\n    if [[ ${#dupes[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then\n        RULE_STATUS=\"$verdict\"\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"d178b4","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_274a72a2eece4e24a4fc73f4bbfa31bc","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"total 128\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 michelkerkmeester  staff    320 25 Oct 13:46 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 25 Oct 13:43 ..\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   5306 25 Oct 13:45 acceptance-criteria.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    571 25 Oct 13:46 description.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   6007 25 Oct 13:46 graph-metadata.json\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   3672 25 Oct 13:43 implementation-summary.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  13797 25 Oct 13:45 plan.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 25 Oct 13:43 scratch\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   9455 25 Oct 13:45 spec.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  11502 25 Oct 13:45 tasks.md\n=== scratch\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff   96 25 Oct 13:43 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 michelkerkmeester  staff  320 25 Oct 13:46 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    0 25 Oct 13:43 .gitkeep\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"6c05b4","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
